      en: "Idiofa was a key battleground during the 1964 Simba rebellion, when rebel forces controlled the town for months. Government troops recaptured it after heavy fighting, causing widespread destruction and civilian casualties. The rebellion was part of the post-independence civil wars in Congo. Today, a simple memorial marks the site. Idiofa has since become an agricultural hub, producing cassava, peanuts, and maize. The town lacks running water and electricity for most residents. The local market is the economic center. Efforts to promote peace have been ongoing.",
